&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot;
	data-armory-ids=&quot;81908&quot;
	data-armory-81908-stat=&quot;1697&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Accessory&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt; Dragon&#x27;s&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;&#x2F;tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot;
	data-armory-ids=&quot;91048&quot;
	data-armory-91048-stat=&quot;1697&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Accessory&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt; Dragon&#x27;s&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;&#x2F;tr&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;tbody&gt;&lt;&#x2F;table&gt;
&lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Trinkets&lt;&#x2F;th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Type&lt;&#x2F;th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Stat&lt;&#x2F;th&gt;&lt;&#x2F;tr&gt;&lt;&#x2F;thead&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot;
	data-armory-ids=&quot;93105&quot;
	data-armory-93105-stat=&quot;1697&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Ring&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt; Dragon&#x27;s&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;&#x2F;tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot;
	data-armory-ids=&quot;91234&quot;
	data-armory-91234-stat=&quot;1697&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Ring&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt; Dragon&#x27;s&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;&#x2F;tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot;
	data-armory-ids=&quot;100527&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Relic&lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;td&gt; Brawler &lt;&#x2F;td&gt;&lt;&#x2F;tr&gt;&lt;&#x2F;tbody&gt;&lt;&#x2F;table&gt;
&lt;hr&#x2F;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alternatively, you can use Berserker&#x27;s pants + Dragon&#x27;s weapon to do ever so slightly more damage, but berserker weapons are far more commonly used.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;weapon-swap&quot;&gt;Weapon Swap&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Weapon swap is optional, all the available options will reduce DPS and lock you out of hammer, they should be prioritised based on utility requirements.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Greatsword - Provides a long range, short cooldown leap and an AoE pull. Does decent burst damage with 4+2, but the sustained dps is far lower than hammer&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bow - Bow provides a ranged option for bosses with melee DPS downtime, but can only reach 24k~ dps with this build.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Optimised Loadout
&lt;a rel=&quot;noopener&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;gw2skills.net&#x2F;editor&#x2F;?PWiAIFlJwmYZMO2JO0L+tVA-DSRYBRFMH+zoWpaFqKZ+DIAhqHeNU4MCUB-e&quot;&gt;GW2Skills Link&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;food&quot;&gt;Food&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;91805&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Cilantro Lime Sous-Vide Steak OR&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;41569&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Bowl of Sweet and Spicy Butternut Squash Soup&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;utility&quot;&gt;Utility&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;items&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9443&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Superior Sharpening Stone&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;build&quot;&gt;Build&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Power DPS&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;pre data-lang=&quot;chatlink&quot; class=&quot;language-chatlink z-code&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-chatlink&quot; data-lang=&quot;chatlink&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;z-source z-chatlink&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;z-punctuation z-definition z-string z-begin&quot;&gt;[&amp;amp;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;DQEqOhA+Gys4AQMB&#x2F;gAAABYBAABLAQAAcRIAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACMwAyAAA=&lt;span class=&quot;z-punctuation z-definition z-string z-end&quot;&gt;]&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;span&gt;&lt;&#x2F;code&gt;&lt;&#x2F;pre&gt;
&lt;hr &#x2F;&gt;
&lt;div data-armory-embed=&#x27;skills&#x27; data-armory-ids=&#x27;9158,9093,9128,9253,30461&#x27;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;div&gt;&lt;div data-armory-embed=&#x27;specializations&#x27; data-armory-ids=&#x27;42,16,27&#x27; data-armory-42-traits=&#x27;634,653,2017&#x27; data-armory-16-traits=&#x27;566,565,1683&#x27; data-armory-27-traits=&#x27;1911,1835,1963&#x27;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;rotation-and-utilities&quot;&gt;Rotation and Utilities&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;alternative-utilities&quot;&gt;Alternative Utilities&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This build is heavily reliant on resolution 100% uptime, which can be reached with &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9253&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Hallowed Ground and &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9085&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Save Yourselves!&quot; alone.
&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9153&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Stand Your Ground!&quot; also provides resolution, but not enough for 100% uptime unless your sub is providing enough to cover the 4~ second downtime.
If your sub is providing 100% uptime on resolution, you can flex both slots, however its important to avoid anything with a cast time.
Even the most damaging utility skills are a DPS loss compared to hammer 1.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9253&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Hallowed Ground provides pulsing group stability, and pulsing resolution, but results in a small DPS loss due to its cast time.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9085&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Save Yourselves!&quot; provides the all important resolution, among other boons, stuns breaks, and steals condis from allies.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9153&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Stand Your Ground!&quot; provides resolution, group stability, and group stun break.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9084&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Advance!&quot; for lots of extra group aegis&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9245&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Smite Condition for a decent DPS boost, provided your sub has resolution uptime covered.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9247&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Judge&#x27;s Intervention for boss fights that require you to travel alot. 1200-range gap-closer and stunbreak with a 20s cooldown.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;elite-skill&quot;&gt;Elite Skill&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;30461&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Signet of Courage is the default option. This should only ever be used as an emergency stun break or group stability. It has a long channel, but this can be interrupted at any point by simply moving.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;29965&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Feel My Wrath!&quot; Can be nice for a little superspeed, and to cover a little quickness if you are separated from your boons.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;30273&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Dragon&#x27;s Maw For a little extra CC, and only a tiny DPS loss from its cast time.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;dps-rotation&quot;&gt;DPS Rotation&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opening - &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9253&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Hallowed Ground and &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9085&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Save Yourselves!&quot;&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9159&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Hammer Swing Hammer auto attack (1)&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Re-use the opening utilities off cooldown to upkeep resolution. If you notice allies are providing resolution, save &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9253&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Hallowed Ground for stability.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ol&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;crowd-control-rotation&quot;&gt;Crowd Control rotation&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9260&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Zealot&#x27;s Embrace (Hammer 3),  &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9124&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Banish (Hammer 4), and &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9195&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Ring of Warding (Hammer 5) are all pretty good CC options.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;30225&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Wings of Resolve (Traited F2) also provides immobilize.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;29887&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Spear of Justice -&amp;gt; &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;33134&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Hunter&#x27;s Verdict will also do CC, however this should be your last CC option, as losing the justice passive temporarily may drop your DPS.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9128&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Sanctuary can be used in the flex slot for huge CC, if resolution uptime is covered by allies.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;sustainability&quot;&gt;Sustainability&lt;&#x2F;h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your autos generate perma-protection.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;30039&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; Shield of Courage provides aegis, a stun break, as well as a decently long block duration that doesn&#x27;t prevent you from attacking.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use &lt;span class=&quot;armory-inline&quot; data-armory-embed=&quot;skills&quot; data-armory-ids=&quot;9153&quot;&gt;&lt;&#x2F;span&gt; &quot;Stand Your Ground!&quot; for a group stun break and multiple stacks of stability.&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
</content>
        
